is a port of the Gentoo Distribution to  the Zaurus PDA.  It can be
mounted over NFS so no  changes to a current configuration are needed. It
includes a native gcc environment for the ARM CPU, the zgcc-3.3.1 cross
compiler for the main PC with distcc configured so that  the main PC does
the actual compiling, and X11 for  testing applications. See TuxMobil.org
for more information about Linux on PDAs and handheld computers[2].

